1
00:00:01,966 --> 00:00:05,966
To most of us,
snakes shout danger!

2
00:00:05,966 --> 00:00:08,966
And that's a valuable instinct.

3
00:00:08,966 --> 00:00:13,566
Every year, they bite
over five million people.

4
00:00:17,566 --> 00:00:20,566
Some have lethal venom,

5
00:00:20,566 --> 00:00:23,066
others primal aggression.

6
00:00:23,066 --> 00:00:26,133
A handful have both.

7
00:00:29,632 --> 00:00:32,632
Which snake is the most dangerous?

8
00:00:32,632 --> 00:00:35,632
It's the one in front of you.

9
00:00:35,632 --> 00:00:37,132
What are your chances?

10
00:00:37,132 --> 00:00:40,799
We'll tally them up
and tell you.

11
00:00:43,132 --> 00:00:45,300
World's Deadliest Snakes.

12
00:00:48,832 --> 00:00:50,332
Australia.

13
00:00:50,332 --> 00:00:51,832
India.

14
00:00:51,832 --> 00:00:55,332
But first, Southeast Asia.

15
00:00:55,332 --> 00:01:00,665
A hot spot for some
of the world's deadliest snakes.

16
00:01:08,133 --> 00:01:12,166
The humid tropical rain forests
of Indonesia.

17
00:01:14,032 --> 00:01:16,682
A hunting ground for one
of the biggest

18
00:01:16,682 --> 00:01:19,333
and most powerful snakes
in the world.

19
00:01:21,032 --> 00:01:24,865
♪ ♪

20
00:01:30,899 --> 00:01:33,899
It's a reticulated python,

21
00:01:33,899 --> 00:01:37,399
longer than a London bus.

22
00:01:37,399 --> 00:01:41,399
No venom, but a bad temper,

23
00:01:41,399 --> 00:01:44,399
350 pounds of it.

24
00:01:54,133 --> 00:01:57,133
Such a colossal predator

25
00:01:57,133 --> 00:02:00,133
requires a man-sized meal.

26
00:02:00,133 --> 00:02:03,133
Usually hunting at night,

27
00:02:03,133 --> 00:02:06,633
the python's reticulated camouflage

28
00:02:06,633 --> 00:02:11,633
allows it to move around
the jungle

29
00:02:11,633 --> 00:02:14,633
unnoticed in the day.

30
00:02:26,865 --> 00:02:31,467
Despite its enormous size,
this giant is surprisingly active.

31
00:02:35,965 --> 00:02:39,965
Even primates are
a welcome appetizer.

32
00:02:39,965 --> 00:02:43,965
In the wild it can hunt anywhere,

33
00:02:43,965 --> 00:02:48,965
but water helps support
its massive bulk.

34
00:02:52,433 --> 00:02:56,433
It's capable of staying submerged

35
00:02:56,433 --> 00:02:59,933
for up to 20 minutes.

36
00:02:59,933 --> 00:03:03,433
You'll never see it coming.

37
00:03:03,433 --> 00:03:08,433
These jungle streams provide
this giant python

38
00:03:08,433 --> 00:03:13,433
a direct express lane
into human settlements.

39
00:03:13,433 --> 00:03:18,933
Southeast Asia is home
to over 655 million people,

40
00:03:19,933 --> 00:03:24,433
and many communities border
the python's rain forests.

41
00:03:25,433 --> 00:03:30,433
It's not unknown for pets
to go missing,

42
00:03:30,433 --> 00:03:33,433
and sometimes children.

43
00:03:37,032 --> 00:03:41,032
Night gives the python
the advantage.

44
00:03:41,032 --> 00:03:46,032
Cat-like eyes are optimized
for night vision.

45
00:03:46,032 --> 00:03:49,532
And those pits along its snout

46
00:03:49,532 --> 00:03:54,532
detect the body heat
of warm-blooded prey.

47
00:04:01,999 --> 00:04:10,166
♪ ♪

48
00:04:13,732 --> 00:04:16,732
Once locked in its jaws,

49
00:04:16,732 --> 00:04:22,232
around 100 recurved teeth
make escape near impossible.

50
00:04:22,232 --> 00:04:24,732
Squeezing so tight,

51
00:04:24,732 --> 00:04:29,732
it stops their blood flowing
within minutes.

52
00:04:29,732 --> 00:04:33,932
Flexible bones and ligaments
allow the python

53
00:04:34,732 --> 00:04:38,132
to spread its mouth
wider than its skull.

54
00:04:43,765 --> 00:04:47,599
This meal is the size
of a child.

55
00:04:49,832 --> 00:04:55,032
A serious problem when a hungry
python ventures into a village.

56
00:04:55,832 --> 00:05:00,832
The reticulated python's fear
and aggression factors are high,

57
00:05:01,832 --> 00:05:06,832
but it's all brute strength,
without the venom.

58
00:05:06,832 --> 00:05:10,332
Bites are devastating, but rare.

59
00:05:10,332 --> 00:05:13,332
Unless you're a small child,

60
00:05:13,332 --> 00:05:17,832
your chances of survival
are high.

61
00:05:21,866 --> 00:05:24,866
When it comes to snakes,

62
00:05:24,866 --> 00:05:30,366
you don't always have to be big
to be deadly.

63
00:05:31,366 --> 00:05:34,366
India, China and Indonesia,

64
00:05:34,366 --> 00:05:38,566
famous for coffee, tea,
and venomous reptiles.

65
00:05:39,366 --> 00:05:44,366
Hidden within the leaves
are small, arboreal snakes

66
00:05:44,366 --> 00:05:47,366
that terrify local farmers.

67
00:05:47,366 --> 00:05:49,866
Green pit vipers.

68
00:05:49,866 --> 00:05:53,866
They don't mean
to harm humans.

69
00:05:53,866 --> 00:05:59,066
It's a by-product of their
incredible hunting prowess.

70
00:05:59,066 --> 00:06:03,866
Like the python, they use
heat-sensing pit organs

71
00:06:03,866 --> 00:06:07,866
on either side of their heads

72
00:06:07,866 --> 00:06:12,866
to track warm-blooded prey
like birds and rats.

73
00:06:15,932 --> 00:06:17,966
♪ ♪

74
00:06:20,699 --> 00:06:24,699
That wide head houses
large venom glands

75
00:06:24,699 --> 00:06:27,899
and long, hinged fangs.

76
00:06:30,732 --> 00:06:33,232
Like other vipers,
their mouths

77
00:06:33,232 --> 00:06:36,232
can open almost 180 degrees
to strike.

78
00:06:36,232 --> 00:06:39,532
But their venom isn't
the worst of them.

79
00:06:39,532 --> 00:06:41,532
Green pit vipers are dangerous

80
00:06:41,532 --> 00:06:44,032
because these tree-dwellers hunt

81
00:06:44,032 --> 00:06:45,832
and strike at head height.

82
00:06:45,832 --> 00:06:48,232
A mistaken bite on a human

83
00:06:48,232 --> 00:06:51,232
can cause bleeding
and painful swelling,

84
00:06:51,232 --> 00:06:55,732
sometimes resulting
in asphyxiation and death.

85
00:06:57,965 --> 00:07:01,465
They account for more snakebites

86
00:07:01,465 --> 00:07:06,965
than any other group
in all of Southeast Asia.

87
00:07:06,965 --> 00:07:10,965
And they have another
tag-team cousin

88
00:07:10,965 --> 00:07:13,465
at work below.

89
00:07:13,465 --> 00:07:16,965
There's a more venomous viper

90
00:07:16,965 --> 00:07:19,965
lurking in the leaf litter.

91
00:07:19,965 --> 00:07:22,965
A snake that's responsible

92
00:07:22,965 --> 00:07:26,467
for several hundred snakebites
every year.

93
00:07:28,799 --> 00:07:31,299
The Malayan pit viper.

94
00:07:31,299 --> 00:07:34,299
Palm oil and rubber plantations

95
00:07:34,299 --> 00:07:37,799
pepper the jungles
of Southeast Asia.

96
00:07:37,799 --> 00:07:42,299
Great places for a snake
to hunt rodents.

97
00:07:42,299 --> 00:07:45,299
Its strategy is
to bite immediately,

98
00:07:45,299 --> 00:07:48,299
injecting fast-acting,
hemotoxic venom,

99
00:07:48,299 --> 00:07:50,799
which causes severe pain,

100
00:07:50,799 --> 00:07:54,299
extensive necrosis
and massive internal bleeding.

101
00:07:54,299 --> 00:07:56,799
Its venom is so effective,

102
00:07:56,799 --> 00:08:00,299
its anticoagulant properties
are being researched

103
00:08:00,299 --> 00:08:03,799
as potential treatment
for stroke victims.

104
00:08:03,799 --> 00:08:07,799
While its cousins,
the green pit vipers,

105
00:08:07,799 --> 00:08:10,299
take care of the trees,

106
00:08:10,299 --> 00:08:14,299
the Malayan pit viper
covers the ground,

107
00:08:14,299 --> 00:08:18,299
lying in wait for rodents
and frogs.

108
00:08:18,299 --> 00:08:22,299
Its pointed, leaf-shaped head
and mottled markings

109
00:08:22,299 --> 00:08:26,799
help it blend perfectly
into the leaf litter.

110
00:08:26,799 --> 00:08:28,799
Invisible.

111
00:08:28,799 --> 00:08:31,799
So easy to step on.

112
00:08:33,193 --> 00:08:37,693
These fangs can breach
a rubber boot.

113
00:08:37,693 --> 00:08:41,193
Due to the lack of antivenom

114
00:08:41,193 --> 00:08:45,193
and hospital treatment
in rural Southeast Asia,

115
00:08:45,193 --> 00:08:48,693
those that survive
are often left

116
00:08:48,693 --> 00:08:51,693
with dysfunctional
or amputated limbs,

117
00:08:51,693 --> 00:08:55,193
which is why it's
locally nicknamed

118
00:08:55,193 --> 00:08:57,266
the "axe snake."

119
00:08:58,966 --> 00:09:02,966
It's time to tally up
our first contenders

120
00:09:02,966 --> 00:09:06,966
for the title of the Indo-Pacific's
deadliest snake.

121
00:09:06,966 --> 00:09:10,466
The pit vipers' venoms
are potent enough

122
00:09:10,466 --> 00:09:14,466
to devastate limbs,
and they're quick to strike.

123
00:09:14,466 --> 00:09:18,466
Yet, despite being responsible
for hundreds of thousands

124
00:09:18,466 --> 00:09:20,466
of bites each year,

125
00:09:20,466 --> 00:09:22,466
only 2% are fatal.

126
00:09:22,466 --> 00:09:24,966
But it's more than enough

127
00:09:24,966 --> 00:09:28,966
to beat the giant python
off top spot,

128
00:09:28,966 --> 00:09:30,400
for now.

129
00:09:33,799 --> 00:09:35,299
India.

130
00:09:35,299 --> 00:09:39,799
Home to four of the world's
deadliest snakes

131
00:09:39,799 --> 00:09:43,299
and nearly 1.4 billion people.

132
00:09:43,299 --> 00:09:47,799
Over four times the population
of the US,

133
00:09:47,799 --> 00:09:51,799
in a country smaller
than the West Coast.

134
00:09:51,799 --> 00:09:56,299
A myriad of people
and a host of dangerous snakes;

135
00:09:56,299 --> 00:09:58,799
a recipe for disaster.

136
00:09:58,799 --> 00:10:03,299
One of the most venomous
is the common krait.

137
00:10:03,299 --> 00:10:06,799
It's small, slender
and unassuming.

138
00:10:06,799 --> 00:10:10,799
Yet its venom,
meant to immobilize prey,

139
00:10:10,799 --> 00:10:14,299
can cause respiratory arrest
in humans.

140
00:10:14,299 --> 00:10:18,333
Just one bite
can kill seven people.

141
00:10:18,333 --> 00:10:24,566
Shy, docile, and slow by day.

142
00:10:29,132 --> 00:10:33,132
At night,
the krait transforms

143
00:10:33,132 --> 00:10:37,632
into an alert
and active hunter.

144
00:10:37,632 --> 00:10:40,632
During the rainy season,

145
00:10:40,632 --> 00:10:45,632
it enters homes
in search of shelter,

146
00:10:45,632 --> 00:10:48,132
warmth, and reptiles.

147
00:10:56,132 --> 00:11:01,066
Rolling the wrong way
could be fatal.

148
00:11:05,232 --> 00:11:07,032
The common krait's bite

149
00:11:07,032 --> 00:11:08,699
is so small and painless,

150
00:11:08,699 --> 00:11:10,699
it feels like a mosquito bite.

151
00:11:13,133 --> 00:11:16,133
In a matter of hours,

152
00:11:16,133 --> 00:11:20,133
full-body paralysis sets in
and maybe death.

153
00:11:20,133 --> 00:11:23,666
Many bite victims
simply never wake up.

154
00:11:25,599 --> 00:11:29,599
The common krait is a problem
in India,

155
00:11:29,599 --> 00:11:33,099
but there's an even more
dangerous killer

156
00:11:33,099 --> 00:11:35,400
that haunts India's farmlands.

157
00:11:38,799 --> 00:11:43,299
An ambush predator,
known as the lurker.

158
00:11:43,299 --> 00:11:47,299
A snake that is near-impossible
to see,

159
00:11:47,299 --> 00:11:49,300
until it's too late.

160
00:11:52,999 --> 00:11:56,100
The highly venomous
Russell's viper.

161
00:11:59,632 --> 00:12:02,632
One of the most dangerous snakes

162
00:12:02,632 --> 00:12:05,132
in all of Asia.

163
00:12:05,132 --> 00:12:08,132
This large, stocky,
slow-moving snake

164
00:12:08,132 --> 00:12:10,632
is a master of camouflage.

165
00:12:10,632 --> 00:12:12,132
Notoriously defensive,

166
00:12:12,132 --> 00:12:14,632
it often holds its ground

167
00:12:14,632 --> 00:12:18,366
and gets stepped on
by accident.

168
00:12:24,632 --> 00:12:28,632
Not only do people
not see it,

169
00:12:28,632 --> 00:12:32,132
but its strikes are so quick,

170
00:12:32,132 --> 00:12:35,132
there's no time to react.

171
00:12:43,066 --> 00:12:46,066
Its large, flattened head
accommodates

172
00:12:46,566 --> 00:12:50,066
two long, half-inch,
hinged fangs,

173
00:12:50,066 --> 00:12:54,566
which deliver huge doses
of potent cytotoxic venom.

174
00:12:55,066 --> 00:12:58,566
A bite causes
excruciating pain

175
00:12:58,566 --> 00:13:01,066
and begins destroying flesh.

176
00:13:01,066 --> 00:13:03,566
It's a predatory masterpiece,

177
00:13:03,566 --> 00:13:08,066
but what makes the Russell's viper
so dangerous

178
00:13:08,566 --> 00:13:12,566
is its penchant
for entering human settlements.

179
00:13:13,066 --> 00:13:14,566
Why?

180
00:13:14,566 --> 00:13:16,566
They're not malicious,

181
00:13:16,566 --> 00:13:19,566
they're just after rats.

182
00:13:19,566 --> 00:13:23,066
Out here,
there are no hospitals,

183
00:13:23,566 --> 00:13:28,066
and antivenom,
even if you can find it,

184
00:13:28,566 --> 00:13:30,566
isn't always effective.

185
00:13:30,566 --> 00:13:36,066
So, bites claim thousands
of limbs and lives every year.

186
00:13:36,199 --> 00:13:39,066
Arch-enemy,
or valuable service provider?

187
00:13:44,999 --> 00:13:47,499
Pest control.

188
00:14:07,300 --> 00:14:09,300
Rodents bite back,

189
00:14:09,300 --> 00:14:12,300
so the viper and its venom

190
00:14:12,300 --> 00:14:14,367
have a nifty plan.

191
00:14:16,598 --> 00:14:19,098
Bite......

192
00:14:19,098 --> 00:14:21,598
And release.

193
00:14:35,333 --> 00:14:39,333
Large glands at the back
of its head

194
00:14:39,333 --> 00:14:43,333
yield enough venom
to kill over 600 mice

195
00:14:43,333 --> 00:14:45,333
from a single bite.

196
00:14:45,333 --> 00:14:49,333
The common krait and this,
the Russell's viper,

197
00:14:49,333 --> 00:14:53,833
are considered two of
the deadliest snakes on Earth.

198
00:14:53,833 --> 00:14:57,833
But how do they score
against each other?

199
00:14:57,833 --> 00:15:01,333
The common krait
is reluctant to bite,

200
00:15:01,333 --> 00:15:04,333
but when it does,
it injects

201
00:15:04,333 --> 00:15:09,033
one of the most potently
toxic venoms in the world.

202
00:15:09,033 --> 00:15:10,833
Found throughout India,

203
00:15:10,833 --> 00:15:15,833
it's responsible for tens of
thousands of bites each year,

204
00:15:15,833 --> 00:15:20,099
and if left untreated,
80% of its victims die.

205
00:15:20,099 --> 00:15:23,599
But does the Russell's viper
have the edge?

206
00:15:23,599 --> 00:15:26,099
Its venom glands are larger,

207
00:15:26,099 --> 00:15:29,599
injecting higher doses
of lethal venom.

208
00:15:29,599 --> 00:15:33,099
And due to its wide distribution
around India,

209
00:15:33,099 --> 00:15:35,099
and highly defensive demeanor,

210
00:15:35,099 --> 00:15:38,099
the Russell's viper
is responsible

211
00:15:38,099 --> 00:15:42,599
for more snakebites
than any other snake in the country,

212
00:15:42,599 --> 00:15:44,599
killing thousands every year.

213
00:15:44,599 --> 00:15:46,599
Despite its lethal potential,

214
00:15:46,599 --> 00:15:50,599
the common krait's small fangs
and low venom yield

215
00:15:50,599 --> 00:15:52,599
cost it first place,

216
00:15:52,599 --> 00:15:57,599
making way for the Russell's viper
to take pole position.

217
00:15:59,199 --> 00:16:02,199
To find a worthy challenger,

218
00:16:02,199 --> 00:16:05,199
we must travel
to the country

219
00:16:05,199 --> 00:16:09,699
with the deadliest wildlife
in the world: Australia.

220
00:16:09,699 --> 00:16:13,199
The land of sun, surf,
and snakes.

221
00:16:13,199 --> 00:16:17,499
Here, there is a dangerous snake
for every habitat,

222
00:16:17,499 --> 00:16:21,566
but one in particular is found
all across Australia.

223
00:16:25,698 --> 00:16:28,198
A snake so feared,

224
00:16:28,198 --> 00:16:32,198
it's simply called
the death adder.

225
00:16:32,198 --> 00:16:35,198
And it's hard to spot.

226
00:16:35,198 --> 00:16:39,198
Its patterns and colorations
mimic its surroundings;

227
00:16:39,198 --> 00:16:40,598
dry, arid deserts,

228
00:16:40,598 --> 00:16:43,599
or the undergrowth
of Australia's woodlands.

229
00:16:47,033 --> 00:16:49,533
There it is.

230
00:16:49,533 --> 00:16:53,533
You only notice the death adder

231
00:16:53,533 --> 00:16:58,033
when it moves through the forest,

232
00:16:58,033 --> 00:17:02,533
crossing roads or entering
people's backyards.

233
00:17:06,299 --> 00:17:09,799
The minute it stops,
it vanishes.

234
00:17:09,799 --> 00:17:12,299
It can lie in wait,

235
00:17:12,299 --> 00:17:15,799
submerged in the leaf litter,
motionless,

236
00:17:15,799 --> 00:17:18,299
for days at a time,

237
00:17:18,299 --> 00:17:21,532
primed for an explosive attack.

238
00:17:24,932 --> 00:17:27,932
But first, a trick.

239
00:17:27,932 --> 00:17:32,432
Is that a worm,
or a tail?

240
00:17:40,099 --> 00:17:43,599
Once inquisitive prey
is within range,

241
00:17:43,599 --> 00:17:46,099
this passive hunter unleashes

242
00:17:46,099 --> 00:17:48,599
the fastest strike
in Australia,

243
00:17:48,599 --> 00:17:51,966
under a tenth of a second.

244
00:18:05,732 --> 00:18:09,732
What makes this efficient hunter

245
00:18:09,732 --> 00:18:12,732
so dangerous to humans

246
00:18:12,732 --> 00:18:17,166
are its defensive strikes
on pets and people.

247
00:18:23,932 --> 00:18:30,933
Innocently lying in ambush,
often stepped on by unwary hikers.

248
00:18:33,332 --> 00:18:35,832
Its large, quarter-inch fangs,

249
00:18:35,832 --> 00:18:39,332
swift strike and high venom yield

250
00:18:39,332 --> 00:18:41,332
can inflict serious damage.

251
00:18:41,332 --> 00:18:43,332
Potent, neurotoxic venom

252
00:18:43,332 --> 00:18:46,500
can kill a human
within six hours.

253
00:18:48,632 --> 00:18:52,632
You may make it past them...

254
00:18:55,632 --> 00:18:58,632
But dogs often don't,

255
00:18:58,632 --> 00:19:03,132
succumbing to bites
in just 20 minutes,

256
00:19:03,132 --> 00:19:06,132
regardless of antivenom treatment.

257
00:19:14,433 --> 00:19:16,933
One bite from a death adder

258
00:19:16,933 --> 00:19:19,933
holds enough venom
to kill over 18 people.

259
00:19:19,933 --> 00:19:22,933
And its strike is super fast
and aggressive.

260
00:19:22,933 --> 00:19:25,933
But hidden in the wilds
of Australia,

261
00:19:25,933 --> 00:19:30,433
hikers are the most at risk
of stepping on one,

262
00:19:30,433 --> 00:19:33,933
and while many pets are killed
each year,

263
00:19:33,933 --> 00:19:35,966
nearly all humans survive.

264
00:19:39,233 --> 00:19:41,733
The death adder
is more defensive

265
00:19:41,733 --> 00:19:43,833
and potent than the pit vipers,

266
00:19:43,833 --> 00:19:47,533
but widely accessible medical care
and antivenom

267
00:19:47,533 --> 00:19:49,500
costs it a higher ranking.

268
00:19:53,566 --> 00:19:57,066
Thousands of miles
from the coast,

269
00:19:57,066 --> 00:20:00,566
deep in the outback
of central Australia

270
00:20:00,566 --> 00:20:04,565
is a snake
with a fierce reputation.

271
00:20:10,765 --> 00:20:14,765
The rare and reclusive
inland taipan,

272
00:20:14,765 --> 00:20:19,765
the most potently venomous snake
on the planet.

273
00:20:19,765 --> 00:20:21,265
Why?

274
00:20:21,265 --> 00:20:24,265
Life out here is tough.

275
00:20:24,265 --> 00:20:26,265
To find food,

276
00:20:26,265 --> 00:20:31,265
this large, six-foot snake
can't sit and wait,

277
00:20:31,265 --> 00:20:33,265
it must hunt.

278
00:20:56,199 --> 00:21:00,733
It carries highly specialized
neuro- and hemotoxic venom.

279
00:21:03,333 --> 00:21:08,100
♪ ♪

280
00:21:11,933 --> 00:21:14,933
If this rat gets away,

281
00:21:14,933 --> 00:21:18,933
it may not see another
for days.

282
00:21:18,933 --> 00:21:22,933
To make sure,
it can inject

283
00:21:22,933 --> 00:21:26,933
40,000 times the amount
of venom

284
00:21:26,933 --> 00:21:29,933
necessary to kill the rat.

285
00:21:29,933 --> 00:21:31,433
Awesome?

286
00:21:31,433 --> 00:21:32,933
Maybe not.

287
00:21:32,933 --> 00:21:35,933
Just one of those bites

288
00:21:35,933 --> 00:21:40,433
is enough to kill
over 100 people.

289
00:21:40,433 --> 00:21:44,933
Prey suffer seizures,
paralysis, and internal bleeding,

290
00:21:44,933 --> 00:21:46,933
all within seconds.

291
00:21:46,933 --> 00:21:49,665
And no chance of escape.

292
00:21:55,565 --> 00:21:58,865
This arid desert is
no place to dawdle.

293
00:21:58,865 --> 00:22:00,865
With little shade,

294
00:22:00,865 --> 00:22:04,365
temperatures can soar
over 100 degrees Fahrenheit,

295
00:22:04,365 --> 00:22:06,865
but the taipan has adapted

296
00:22:06,865 --> 00:22:10,365
by changing the color
of its skin.

297
00:22:10,365 --> 00:22:12,865
They lighten in summer,

298
00:22:12,865 --> 00:22:15,365
so as not to overheat,

299
00:22:15,365 --> 00:22:18,565
and darken
during the cooler months,

300
00:22:18,565 --> 00:22:20,565
to retain warmth.

301
00:22:20,565 --> 00:22:24,065
For shelter, the taipan
makes good use

302
00:22:24,065 --> 00:22:27,565
of any unoccupied burrows
and deep cracks

303
00:22:27,565 --> 00:22:29,565
in the dry plains.

304
00:22:29,565 --> 00:22:33,966
It's also the perfect place
to hide eggs.

305
00:22:38,233 --> 00:22:42,233
Newborn taipans
are five times smaller

306
00:22:42,233 --> 00:22:46,233
than the adults,
but also deadly.

307
00:22:46,233 --> 00:22:50,733
Once free, they must
fend for themselves,

308
00:22:50,733 --> 00:22:54,467
with only their venom
to protect them.

309
00:22:56,799 --> 00:22:59,799
But there is one predator

310
00:22:59,799 --> 00:23:04,032
that's immune to even
the taipan's bite.

311
00:23:08,999 --> 00:23:11,799
They call it the mulga.

312
00:23:15,332 --> 00:23:17,832
10 Feet long,

313
00:23:17,832 --> 00:23:20,832
13 pounds in bulk,

314
00:23:20,832 --> 00:23:25,332
it's Australia's heaviest
venomous snake.

315
00:23:25,332 --> 00:23:28,332
Hence its common name,

316
00:23:28,332 --> 00:23:30,832
the king brown.

317
00:23:41,033 --> 00:23:43,533
It's a hunter of snakes,

318
00:23:43,533 --> 00:23:47,033
with immunity to most
of Australia's most venomous,

319
00:23:47,033 --> 00:23:49,233
including the smaller taipan.

320
00:23:52,400 --> 00:23:54,833
♪ ♪

321
00:23:58,433 --> 00:24:00,367
♪ ♪

322
00:24:03,532 --> 00:24:08,032
The king brown's venom may not be
as potent

323
00:24:08,032 --> 00:24:09,532
as the taipan's,

324
00:24:09,532 --> 00:24:12,032
but what it lacks in quality,

325
00:24:12,032 --> 00:24:14,532
it makes up for in quantity,

326
00:24:14,532 --> 00:24:18,032
injecting up to six times
more venom

327
00:24:18,032 --> 00:24:19,532
in a single bite;

328
00:24:19,532 --> 00:24:22,599
the largest venom yield
ever recorded.

329
00:24:25,532 --> 00:24:30,666
Prey suffers hemorrhaging,
paralysis and renal failure.

330
00:24:33,933 --> 00:24:38,433
Australia is home to some of
the world's most venomous snakes,

331
00:24:38,433 --> 00:24:41,433
but how do they rate
against the rest?

332
00:24:41,433 --> 00:24:44,433
The inland taipan
is rightly feared.

333
00:24:44,433 --> 00:24:46,933
Its venom is so potent

334
00:24:46,933 --> 00:24:50,433
that an untreated bite
could kill you

335
00:24:50,433 --> 00:24:52,433
in less than an hour.

336
00:24:52,433 --> 00:24:55,433
But this shy serpent
is relatively placid

337
00:24:55,433 --> 00:24:58,933
and would rather flee
than fight,

338
00:24:58,933 --> 00:25:01,433
so, bites to humans
are uncommon.

339
00:25:01,433 --> 00:25:04,933
Australia is home
to over 25 million people,

340
00:25:04,933 --> 00:25:09,933
but 85% of the population lives
within 30 miles of the coast,

341
00:25:09,933 --> 00:25:13,433
and the inland taipan
hides out

342
00:25:13,433 --> 00:25:17,500
in the middle of the remote
and desolate outback.

343
00:25:17,500 --> 00:25:21,500
Nearly all that are bitten
have survived,

344
00:25:21,500 --> 00:25:24,000
thanks to quick hospitalization.

345
00:25:24,000 --> 00:25:28,500
Which means it may be the world's
most venomous snake,

346
00:25:28,500 --> 00:25:32,500
but the inland taipan
is far from being

347
00:25:32,500 --> 00:25:34,500
the Indo-Pacific's deadliest.

348
00:25:34,500 --> 00:25:38,500
Perhaps the king brown
can kill you quicker?

349
00:25:38,500 --> 00:25:43,500
Its venom may not be as potent
as the taipan's,

350
00:25:43,500 --> 00:25:48,300
but it has a savage bite
and injects enormous amounts.

351
00:25:48,300 --> 00:25:52,300
And being the most widespread
snake in Australia,

352
00:25:52,300 --> 00:25:54,800
bites are much more frequent.

353
00:25:54,800 --> 00:25:57,800
But thanks to localized antivenom,

354
00:25:57,800 --> 00:25:59,000
deaths are rare.

355
00:25:59,000 --> 00:26:01,367
Deadly enough to pip
the taipans.

356
00:26:04,499 --> 00:26:06,999
The king brown
is a heavyweight,

357
00:26:06,999 --> 00:26:10,199
but to find the true king
of deadly snakes,

358
00:26:10,199 --> 00:26:13,699
we must travel to the jungles
of Southeast Asia.

359
00:26:17,366 --> 00:26:19,966
These are the hunting grounds

360
00:26:19,966 --> 00:26:22,933
for the longest venomous snake
in the world.

361
00:26:33,299 --> 00:26:35,732
♪ ♪

362
00:26:40,932 --> 00:26:43,132
The king cobra can stand up

363
00:26:43,132 --> 00:26:45,500
and look you in the eyes.

364
00:26:48,799 --> 00:26:52,099
Using up to 20 pounds
of pure muscle

365
00:26:52,099 --> 00:26:55,100
to raise its body four foot
off the ground.

366
00:26:57,466 --> 00:27:01,466
Like most cobras,
it can flatten its ribs,

367
00:27:01,466 --> 00:27:04,532
extending the looser skin
on its neck.

368
00:27:06,299 --> 00:27:11,299
This colossus can easily live
for 20 years

369
00:27:11,299 --> 00:27:15,299
in the wild,
growing up to 18 foot.

370
00:27:32,466 --> 00:27:36,466
Everything about the king
is large,

371
00:27:36,466 --> 00:27:40,966
including its appetite
and its venom load.

372
00:27:40,966 --> 00:27:44,466
One bite can kill an elephant

373
00:27:44,466 --> 00:27:47,466
in just three hours;

374
00:27:47,466 --> 00:27:50,966
a human, in 30 minutes.

375
00:27:50,966 --> 00:27:55,466
But there's a reason
for its deadliness.

376
00:27:55,466 --> 00:28:00,466
It's a voracious hunter
of other big snakes.

377
00:28:05,699 --> 00:28:09,699
While known to feed on small,
venomous kraits

378
00:28:09,699 --> 00:28:11,199
and other cobras,

379
00:28:11,199 --> 00:28:14,199
they usually hunt down
larger species,

380
00:28:14,199 --> 00:28:15,966
even giant pythons.

381
00:28:19,865 --> 00:28:26,266
This 10-foot rat snake
is unaware it's being watched.

382
00:28:39,032 --> 00:28:42,532
Rat snakes often cloak themselves

383
00:28:42,532 --> 00:28:47,032
in the scent
of their last kill,

384
00:28:47,032 --> 00:28:52,032
so other rodents are less likely
to detect them;

385
00:28:52,032 --> 00:28:56,466
a scent the cobra
can easily track.

386
00:29:03,965 --> 00:29:06,965
The king uses its lower jaw

387
00:29:06,965 --> 00:29:10,965
to detect tiny vibrations
on the ground

388
00:29:10,965 --> 00:29:13,899
to home in on its target.

389
00:29:20,032 --> 00:29:21,932
It needs all the venom,

390
00:29:21,932 --> 00:29:24,266
power and size it can muster.

391
00:29:27,099 --> 00:29:29,299
Bad for the rat snake,

392
00:29:29,299 --> 00:29:31,200
and bad for us.

393
00:29:33,300 --> 00:29:36,800
16-Millimeter fangs,
like hypodermic needles,

394
00:29:36,800 --> 00:29:39,800
inject 20 times more venom

395
00:29:39,800 --> 00:29:42,966
than most venomous snakes
in a single bite.

396
00:29:46,032 --> 00:29:51,032
Within minutes, the neurotoxins
stun the nervous system,

397
00:29:51,032 --> 00:29:53,032
paralyzing the body,

398
00:29:53,032 --> 00:29:57,532
shutting down lungs
and damaging brain functions,

399
00:29:57,532 --> 00:30:01,532
while other toxins begin
the digestion process,

400
00:30:01,532 --> 00:30:03,866
from the inside out.

401
00:30:05,598 --> 00:30:08,598
The cobra's backward-facing teeth

402
00:30:08,598 --> 00:30:11,598
help walk the meal down.

403
00:30:21,366 --> 00:30:24,366
A 10-foot rat snake fits nicely

404
00:30:24,366 --> 00:30:26,733
inside an 18-foot cobra.

405
00:30:28,832 --> 00:30:33,332
The king may be the biggest
venomous killer around,

406
00:30:33,332 --> 00:30:36,066
but is it the deadliest
to us?

407
00:30:39,166 --> 00:30:42,366
A single bite from a king cobra

408
00:30:42,366 --> 00:30:46,566
is enough to kill a human
20 times over.

409
00:30:46,566 --> 00:30:49,566
Yet, despite its size
and reputation,

410
00:30:49,566 --> 00:30:51,566
it's not overly aggressive.

411
00:30:51,566 --> 00:30:55,066
But it doesn't hesitate
to defend itself,

412
00:30:55,066 --> 00:30:58,966
biting tens of thousands
of people each year,

413
00:30:58,966 --> 00:31:03,266
which, left untreated, kills
thousands across the Indo-Pacific.

414
00:31:03,266 --> 00:31:07,466
The king competes
with the deadliest on every level,

415
00:31:07,466 --> 00:31:11,166
but its more tolerant attitude
and reluctance to bite

416
00:31:11,166 --> 00:31:13,233
costs it first place.

417
00:31:16,199 --> 00:31:19,699
If the king can't conquer
top spot,

418
00:31:19,699 --> 00:31:23,699
what about an entire family
of Asian cobras?

419
00:31:25,400 --> 00:31:29,100
There are 12 species of cobra

420
00:31:29,100 --> 00:31:31,800
found throughout
the Indo-Pacific,

421
00:31:31,800 --> 00:31:35,000
and they exact a terrible toll

422
00:31:35,000 --> 00:31:38,200
on the people that live here.

423
00:31:38,200 --> 00:31:40,700
Some can spit their venom,

424
00:31:40,700 --> 00:31:43,700
while others rely
on their size,

425
00:31:43,700 --> 00:31:45,632
cunning, and deadly bite.

426
00:31:48,899 --> 00:31:53,399
The monocled cobra is found
across Southeast Asia,

427
00:31:53,399 --> 00:31:56,399
as far west as Thailand.

428
00:31:56,399 --> 00:32:00,399
This large six-foot snake
hunts rodents

429
00:32:00,399 --> 00:32:03,899
around open fields
and rice paddies,

430
00:32:03,899 --> 00:32:06,500
making human contact inevitable.

431
00:32:08,865 --> 00:32:10,365
With a short temper,

432
00:32:10,365 --> 00:32:12,400
it's aggressively defensive.

433
00:32:14,166 --> 00:32:15,966
It gets its name

434
00:32:15,966 --> 00:32:20,566
from the large circle
on the back of its hood,

435
00:32:20,566 --> 00:32:23,766
and its highly potent
neurotoxic venom

436
00:32:23,766 --> 00:32:27,166
is some of the fastest acting
in the world.

437
00:32:31,199 --> 00:32:33,899
But one of Asia's Big Four

438
00:32:33,899 --> 00:32:36,866
is found throughout
the Indian Subcontinent.

439
00:32:39,698 --> 00:32:43,698
It thrives along the edges
of forests,

440
00:32:43,698 --> 00:32:45,698
fields and villages,

441
00:32:45,698 --> 00:32:47,698
especially near water.

442
00:32:54,765 --> 00:32:57,765
Not one, but two circles;

443
00:32:57,765 --> 00:33:00,500
the spectacled cobra.

444
00:33:04,798 --> 00:33:08,798
The spectacled cobra
is highly alert

445
00:33:08,798 --> 00:33:12,298
to movement,
often striking out,

446
00:33:12,298 --> 00:33:14,798
and highly venomous.

447
00:33:14,798 --> 00:33:18,298
Its hood is deeply cupped.

448
00:33:18,298 --> 00:33:22,298
This cobra puts on
a real show.

449
00:33:22,298 --> 00:33:25,798
Those spectacled eyes
are distinct.

450
00:33:25,798 --> 00:33:27,798
Know your enemy.

451
00:33:39,032 --> 00:33:43,532
It's drawn to the edge
of villages

452
00:33:43,532 --> 00:33:46,532
in its search for food.

453
00:33:46,532 --> 00:33:52,032
A bite not only eats away
at your flesh,

454
00:33:52,032 --> 00:33:56,032
but also causes
full-body paralysis,

455
00:33:56,032 --> 00:34:00,032
crippling your ability
to breathe,

456
00:34:00,032 --> 00:34:02,032
within hours.

457
00:34:12,665 --> 00:34:14,665
With food on tap

458
00:34:14,665 --> 00:34:17,165
in and around human dwellings,

459
00:34:17,165 --> 00:34:20,333
the spectacled cobra
is a familiar face.

460
00:34:22,666 --> 00:34:25,666
♪ ♪

461
00:34:28,133 --> 00:34:30,633
This cobra is so feared,

462
00:34:30,633 --> 00:34:33,133
it's worthy of Hindu deity.

463
00:34:33,133 --> 00:34:35,633
But is it deadly enough

464
00:34:35,633 --> 00:34:38,000
to take top spot?

465
00:34:40,999 --> 00:34:43,499
The monocled and
spectacled cobras

466
00:34:43,499 --> 00:34:46,299
have bites to match
their barks.

467
00:34:46,299 --> 00:34:48,299
And death comes quickly.

468
00:34:48,299 --> 00:34:51,499
They are intolerant
and strike on movement,

469
00:34:51,499 --> 00:34:54,299
but what makes them
really deadly

470
00:34:54,299 --> 00:34:55,799
are their numbers.

471
00:34:55,799 --> 00:34:58,599
Unlike the king,
they are found

472
00:34:58,599 --> 00:35:01,399
all across India
and Southeast Asia,

473
00:35:01,399 --> 00:35:03,899
living among
billions of people,

474
00:35:03,899 --> 00:35:05,899
which makes them responsible

475
00:35:05,899 --> 00:35:09,399
for hundreds of thousands
of bites each year.

476
00:35:09,399 --> 00:35:12,599
And with limited antivenom
and hospital care,

477
00:35:12,599 --> 00:35:16,099
many tens of thousands
of their victims die.

478
00:35:20,299 --> 00:35:23,199
Making the monocled
and spectacled cobras

479
00:35:23,199 --> 00:35:25,499
the deadliest snakes
in Asia...

480
00:35:25,499 --> 00:35:26,999
For now.

481
00:35:26,999 --> 00:35:29,999
It will take a serious
contender

482
00:35:29,999 --> 00:35:33,299
to knock the cobras
off the top spot.

483
00:35:33,299 --> 00:35:35,999
But maybe the second most
venomous snake

484
00:35:35,999 --> 00:35:39,066
in the world could do it.

485
00:35:41,899 --> 00:35:43,299
Down under,

486
00:35:43,299 --> 00:35:46,000
many of the deadliest
look alike.

487
00:35:48,599 --> 00:35:50,099
Taipan?

488
00:35:50,099 --> 00:35:51,599
Mulga?

489
00:35:51,599 --> 00:35:53,099
No.

490
00:35:53,099 --> 00:35:56,599
This is an eastern brown.

491
00:36:02,933 --> 00:36:05,933
Responsible for more
snakebite fatalities

492
00:36:05,933 --> 00:36:08,599
in Australia than any other.

493
00:36:10,732 --> 00:36:13,732
Like the taipans,
their venom

494
00:36:13,732 --> 00:36:17,166
has evolved to kill
fast-moving prey quickly.

495
00:36:20,699 --> 00:36:23,699
They, too, are very fast,

496
00:36:23,699 --> 00:36:26,699
actively chasing down
their prey.

497
00:36:34,132 --> 00:36:37,632
But what makes this snake
so dangerous

498
00:36:37,632 --> 00:36:41,632
is that it thrives
in towns and cities

499
00:36:41,632 --> 00:36:44,132
all across the east coast,

500
00:36:44,132 --> 00:36:47,632
in the most populated areas
of Australia.

501
00:36:47,632 --> 00:36:51,632
It can squeeze its narrow,
five-foot, slender body

502
00:36:51,632 --> 00:36:55,399
through tiny gaps in doorways
of homes and sheds.

503
00:37:01,299 --> 00:37:04,799
Like many others
on the leaderboard,

504
00:37:04,799 --> 00:37:08,799
they're only here for the rats,

505
00:37:08,799 --> 00:37:13,299
but that often means
they face us.

506
00:37:13,299 --> 00:37:17,799
If disturbed,
it reveals a calling card:

507
00:37:17,799 --> 00:37:22,299
a signature "S"
for maximum strike force.

508
00:37:22,299 --> 00:37:27,299
That strike comes
at 40 miles an hour,

509
00:37:27,299 --> 00:37:30,799
often with a gaping mouth

510
00:37:30,799 --> 00:37:35,299
to compensate for its short,
fixed fangs,

511
00:37:35,299 --> 00:37:39,299
which usually means
a painless bite

512
00:37:39,299 --> 00:37:42,799
and one that's difficult
to see.

513
00:37:46,066 --> 00:37:49,966
Yet each bite delivers a small
but deadly venom cocktail,

514
00:37:49,966 --> 00:37:53,866
causing progressive paralysis
and uncontrollable bleeding.

515
00:37:53,866 --> 00:37:56,366
Victims can collapse
within minutes,

516
00:37:56,366 --> 00:37:57,966
and if left untreated,

517
00:37:57,966 --> 00:38:01,966
they could be dead
in under half an hour.

518
00:38:01,966 --> 00:38:05,366
The eastern brown's venom
is so toxic,

519
00:38:05,366 --> 00:38:08,766
not even antivenom
can reverse the effects.

520
00:38:08,766 --> 00:38:13,066
It has a short fuse
and attacks with little warning,

521
00:38:13,066 --> 00:38:17,366
making it responsible
for thousands of bites every year.

522
00:38:17,366 --> 00:38:18,966
In the last decade,

523
00:38:18,966 --> 00:38:23,266
60% of Australia's snakebite
deaths were attributed to them.

524
00:38:23,266 --> 00:38:27,566
They have the venom,
the defensiveness and the opportunity,

525
00:38:27,566 --> 00:38:30,166
but thanks to quick
hospitalization,

526
00:38:30,166 --> 00:38:33,266
they just miss out
on the lead.

527
00:38:37,765 --> 00:38:41,765
To be the deadliest,
a snake needs aggression,

528
00:38:41,765 --> 00:38:45,433
a deadly bite, opportunity,
and human vulnerability.

529
00:38:48,665 --> 00:38:52,532
For that, we need
to return to India.

530
00:38:54,532 --> 00:38:59,532
India is home to nearly
one and a half billion people.

531
00:38:59,532 --> 00:39:03,032
Many of which live and work

532
00:39:03,032 --> 00:39:06,532
in the densely populated
rural districts.

533
00:39:06,532 --> 00:39:10,532
Men, women and children
share this open farmland

534
00:39:10,532 --> 00:39:14,032
with four of the world's
deadliest snakes.

535
00:39:14,032 --> 00:39:17,032
We've met three of them.

536
00:39:17,032 --> 00:39:21,333
And each year, close to 50,000
people die here

537
00:39:21,333 --> 00:39:22,833
from snakebites.

538
00:39:25,066 --> 00:39:29,066
That's the equivalent of a town

539
00:39:29,066 --> 00:39:32,566
being wiped out every year.

540
00:39:32,566 --> 00:39:36,066
And most of those deaths

541
00:39:36,066 --> 00:39:39,066
are from the fourth.

542
00:39:39,066 --> 00:39:41,566
The saw-scaled viper.

543
00:39:41,566 --> 00:39:45,566
Many snakes offer
a clear warning

544
00:39:45,566 --> 00:39:47,566
to stay away,

545
00:39:47,566 --> 00:39:52,566
but this one
is a born deceiver.

546
00:39:58,332 --> 00:40:00,832
At only 12 inches long,

547
00:40:00,832 --> 00:40:04,332
the saw-scaled viper
may be small,

548
00:40:04,332 --> 00:40:07,632
but it packs
a serious punch.

549
00:40:07,632 --> 00:40:11,632
Its venom is many times
more potent

550
00:40:11,632 --> 00:40:13,332
than any cobra.

551
00:40:13,332 --> 00:40:15,432
And being highly aggressive,

552
00:40:15,432 --> 00:40:16,733
it strikes readily.

553
00:40:18,799 --> 00:40:21,799
Lightning-fast,
again and again.

554
00:40:27,732 --> 00:40:32,732
When disturbed, they coil up
into strike position,

555
00:40:32,732 --> 00:40:36,732
rubbing their tough, keeled scales
together

556
00:40:36,732 --> 00:40:39,732
to create a sawing sound,

557
00:40:39,732 --> 00:40:41,732
hence the name.

558
00:40:41,732 --> 00:40:44,732
Ignore it at your peril.

559
00:40:44,732 --> 00:40:47,232
The strike comes quick,

560
00:40:47,232 --> 00:40:49,732
and venom soon after.

561
00:40:49,732 --> 00:40:53,732
But what makes this snake
a problem

562
00:40:53,732 --> 00:40:56,732
is its proximity to humans.

563
00:40:59,333 --> 00:41:04,333
The saw-scaled viper is found
across India and Pakistan,

564
00:41:04,333 --> 00:41:08,699
living amongst highly populated
and remote rural farmlands.

565
00:41:10,932 --> 00:41:13,932
Out here,
there is limited access

566
00:41:13,932 --> 00:41:16,432
to hospitals and antivenom,

567
00:41:16,432 --> 00:41:18,932
and victims often rely

568
00:41:18,932 --> 00:41:21,432
on ineffective
traditional remedies.

569
00:41:21,432 --> 00:41:23,932
Globally, the saw-scaled viper

570
00:41:23,932 --> 00:41:26,932
is responsible
for more human deaths

571
00:41:26,932 --> 00:41:29,666
than all other snake species
combined.

572
00:41:31,399 --> 00:41:34,399
Many of which are children.

573
00:41:34,399 --> 00:41:39,399
The viper's small size
and excellent camouflage

574
00:41:39,399 --> 00:41:42,399
makes them hard to see

575
00:41:42,399 --> 00:41:44,899
under leaves and grass.

576
00:41:44,899 --> 00:41:47,399
And unlike the Russell's,

577
00:41:47,399 --> 00:41:50,399
they don't try to flee,

578
00:41:50,399 --> 00:41:53,399
or mock-charge like the king.

579
00:41:53,399 --> 00:41:57,399
Instead, the saw-scaled
stands its ground,

580
00:41:57,399 --> 00:42:00,899
biting at anyone and anything

581
00:42:00,899 --> 00:42:03,399
that comes too close.

582
00:42:17,932 --> 00:42:19,467
Ah!

583
00:42:23,299 --> 00:42:28,299
Within minutes, the victim's limbs
start to swell

584
00:42:28,299 --> 00:42:32,799
as the necrotic venom
breaks down blood vessels

585
00:42:32,799 --> 00:42:36,799
and muscle, often leading
to unavoidable amputations.

586
00:42:36,799 --> 00:42:40,299
If left untreated,
the excruciating pain

587
00:42:40,299 --> 00:42:43,299
is followed by organ failure

588
00:42:43,299 --> 00:42:45,799
and quite easily, death.

589
00:42:45,799 --> 00:42:49,799
It's not the biggest
or the fastest,

590
00:42:49,799 --> 00:42:52,799
or even the most potent,

591
00:42:52,799 --> 00:42:56,299
but it lives on our doorstep,

592
00:42:56,299 --> 00:42:58,299
it's notoriously aggressive,

593
00:42:58,299 --> 00:43:00,799
and it strikes with relish,

594
00:43:00,799 --> 00:43:02,799
which all stacks up

595
00:43:02,799 --> 00:43:05,299
to make the saw-scaled viper

596
00:43:05,299 --> 00:43:09,966
the deadliest snake
across the Indo-Pacific.

597
00:43:14,898 --> 00:43:18,098
These snakes have a bad rap,

598
00:43:18,098 --> 00:43:21,298
but their bites are in defense.

599
00:43:21,298 --> 00:43:23,298
Humans aren't prey

600
00:43:23,298 --> 00:43:27,798
and snakes don't actively
set out to harm us.

601
00:43:27,798 --> 00:43:31,298
A life without limbs
has armed them

602
00:43:31,298 --> 00:43:34,498
with an arsenal
of alternative skills

603
00:43:34,498 --> 00:43:36,798
to master their environments:

604
00:43:36,798 --> 00:43:39,998
chemical weaponry,
highly evolved senses,

605
00:43:39,998 --> 00:43:42,498
and incredible muscle power.

606
00:43:42,498 --> 00:43:45,398
Without them,
rodents would run riot,

607
00:43:45,398 --> 00:43:47,498
agriculture would be plagued,

608
00:43:47,498 --> 00:43:51,033
and our homes would be infested
with disease.

609
00:43:53,500 --> 00:43:57,500
As much as we may fear them,

610
00:43:57,500 --> 00:44:00,500
a world without snakes

611
00:44:00,500 --> 00:44:06,632
would be a far more
dangerous place.

